In article <629@uucs1.UUCP> rfp@uucs1.uucp (Roger F. Powell) writes:
>This group has featured many a (deserved) tribute to the dev team.
>Tonight, I'm in a bad mood, and I feel like pointing out the 10
>worst (mis)features in the game.  Here goes....
>
> 10) Corpses intermingle in your inventory.  Accidentally carry around
>     an old jackal corpse, kill a fresh one, pick it up and eat it...
>     oops - the two are intermingled and you get very sick

I would take issue with your charge of "unfairness", Roger - the merge 
feature -averages- the corpse-ages, so although the new corpse is made
more "stale" by the merge, the old corpse is in effect "freshened" by it, 
and BOTH corpses usually end up being edible (even if the old one was 
*guaranteed* to make you sick!).

It's a fairly easy matter for a player to prevent the merge anyway, by 
#name'ing one of the corpses...

